Read AGENTS.md at the repository root and follow it fully before doing any work.

This project uses a validation-gated, one-story-at-a-time operating system.
AGENTS.md is the entrypoint and defines the binding rules. In particular:

- "Done" means validated live and recorded in governance/RUNBOOK.md — never on
  inference, never because code merged.
- Do the session ritual first: close out the prior story, then check the
  advancement gate (a story cannot start until its dependencies are all done).
- Never self-certify a story as done; the human validates, you record.
- Never push to main directly — branch + PR only.
- End every session by authoring the next story's warm handoff.

See AGENTS.md for the full operating system.
